http://lca2005.linux.org.au/

I'm currently at LCA (see above URL).

http://lca2005.linux.org.au/security_miniconf/

I gave three talks about SE Linux at the security miniconf.  They went 
reasonably well.  In my talk on writing SE Linux policy about half the 
audience left early, this wasn't a great surprise.  When giving a very 
demanding talk at a time when people are about to go to bars you have to 
expect some people to leave early - especially if the talk runs over time.

I've got a play machine on the net for the conference, when tea ladies and 
other people don't turn it off.  :(

As I've given all my talks the rest of the conference will be fairly relaxing 
for me.  I had an interesting conversation with someone from a major company 
who is running SE Linux on FC3 now and looking at RHEL4 for future use.  I 
expect more of the same during the rest of the conference.

